  "outcome": "escalate",
  "rationale": "The claim must be escalated because automated findings indicate it is unclear whether an exclusion applies due to open questions about the driver's condition. Section 6.2 governs this referral when material facts are open to more than one reasonable reading. The key fact is that the claimant reported consuming alcohol before the collision.",
  "citations": [
    {
      "clause_id": "PLUS-6.2",
      "quote": "If the documents submitted do not allow the adjuster to determine whether an exclusion applies, because material facts are disputed, missing or open to more than one reasonable reading, the claim must be escalated for further investigation rather than approved or denied on the information available."
    }
  ]
}
